ore_sbc_dilution":81.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0018799999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alcon Inc. researches, develops, manufactures, distributes, and sells eye care products worldwide. The company operates through two segments, Surgical and Vision Care. It offers equipment, instrumentation and diagnostics, intraocular lenses (IOLs), and other implantables; and consumables, including viscoelastics, surgical solutions, incisional instruments, surgical custom packs, and other products for surgical procedures. The company's cataract products include Unity CS, LenSx laser system, Verion reference unit and Verion digital marker, ARGOS biometer, SMARTCATARACT health platform, NGENUITY 3D visualization system, LuxOR surgical ophthalmic microscope, and ORA system for intra-operative measurements; ADI cloud-based platform; and implantable products, including monofocal, Toric, and Presbyopia-Correcting IOLs, as well as delivery systems, such as AutonoMe and UltraSert. In addition, it provides Custom Pak surgical procedure packs vitreoretinal products comprising constellation vision systems, procedure packs, lasers and hand-held microsurgical instruments, Grieshaber, MIVS instruments; scissors, forceps and micro-instruments, medical grade vitreous tamponades, and Hypervit probes; and refractive surgery products, including WaveLight and Contoura Vision used for LASIK refractive procedure. Further, the company offers daily disposable, reusable, and color-enhancing contact lenses; ocular health products, such as dry eye, ocular allergies, glaucoma, and contact lens care, as well as ocular vitamins and redness relievers. In addition it also develops and commercializes therapies for chronic eye diseases, focusing on encapsulated cell therapy platforms for ocular conditions. The company was formerly known as Alcon Universal S.A. and changed its name to Alcon Inc. in December 2001. Alcon Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in Geneva, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David J. Endicott | CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Alcon Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $37.8B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 61% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 53-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 76% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $2.1B in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Alcidion (ASX:ALC): Will It Rally Now Its Consolidation Is Complete?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/penny/alcidion-asxalc-will-it-rally-now-its-consolidation-is-complete","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795757520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alcidion Group (ASX:ALC): Which Capital Changes Has It Completed?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/penny/alcidion-group-asxalc-which-capital-changes-has-it-completed","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795656060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Orbis International and Alcon Help Peru Hospital Expand Cataract Surgery and Reduce Wait Lists","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/orbis-international-alcon-help-peru-204300492.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795552980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.859,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alcidion Group Limited Completes Purchase of 54,500 Shares on 26 November 2026 Under On-Market Buy-Back Scheme","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/news/announcements/alcidion-group-limited-completes-purchase-of-54500-shares-on-26-november-2026-under-on-market-buy-back-scheme","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795734903.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Australian Healthcare Stocks With Revenue Growth Over 9%","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/3-australian-healthcare-stocks-revenue-220936228